.TH DISKATLAS 1 "2026-11-07" "diskatlas 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
diskatlas \- show where disk space goes, as charts and lists
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diskatlas
.RI [ FOLDER ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B diskatlas
is a graphical, read-only disk usage analyzer.
It scans a folder or a whole volume and shows the result as a sunburst chart,
a treemap, a folder listing and a list of the largest files.
It never changes, moves or deletes anything.
.PP
If
.I FOLDER
is given, the scan starts immediately.
Otherwise the window opens with the folder used last time, or the home directory,
and a scan starts when you choose
.BR Scan .
.SS What a scan includes
A scan stays within the filesystem that holds the starting folder.
It does not enter other mounted filesystems, including bind mounts and pseudo\-filesystems
such as
.IR /proc ;
those folders are listed as empty entries, and the status bar counts the folders skipped
because they are on another device.
Symbolic links are listed but never followed, except when the starting folder itself is a
symbolic link.
A file with several hard links is counted once.
.PP
Folders can be excluded from later scans, either by typing an absolute path under
.B Excluded folders
in the left panel, or with
.B Exclude this folder
in the details panel.
Excluded folders are listed as empty entries.
.PP
Sizes are the sum of file lengths.
Allocated size comes from filesystem blocks and may differ from the space a deletion would
free, especially on filesystems that share data between files, such as Btrfs.
Results are an estimate: files can change while a scan runs.
.SS Interface
The left panel lists mounted volumes with their capacity and has an
.B Appearance
section: theme (system, light, dark or high contrast), interface size, and an option to
reduce motion.
.B Ctrl+plus ,
.B Ctrl+minus
and
.B Ctrl+0
also change the interface size.
.SH OPTIONS
There are no command line options.
The single argument is the folder to scan.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/diskatlas/settings.conf
Saved settings, created with mode 0600.
If
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset or not an absolute path, the file is
.IR ~/.config/diskatlas/settings.conf .
It holds one
.IR key = value
pair per line:
.BR view ,
.BR theme ,
.BR zoom ,
.BR reduced_motion ,
.BR window ,
.B last_folder
and one
.B exclude
line for each excluded folder.
Lines that are not understood are ignored, so the file can be edited by hand.
The window size is written when the program exits.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the settings file.
.TP
.B HOME
Used to find the settings file and as the default folder to scan.
.SH BUGS
Report problems at
.UR https://github.com/mikeholp87/disk-atlas/issues
.UE .
Scan progress shows only the number of entries found.
Cancelling cannot interrupt a filesystem call that is already blocked.
